(R/'final_scientific_interpretation.md').write_text('''# Final scientific interpretation\n\nThe fixed-REF plus fixed-ALT corrected population-level estimates are D1 +0.19955, D2 +0.13186, and D3 +0.08359 over the full chr17 scan. Original fixed-REF-only results (D1 −0.13038, D2 +0.02569, D3 +0.05725) are superseded and retained only as historical comparisons. Corrected inversion union versus full-contig complement is +0.39396 vs +0.04378 (D1), +0.24055 vs +0.02010 (D2), and +0.26206 vs +0.01446 (D3). These are separate from the exact tree matched span (5.0–37.055 Mb): inside/outside D_site is 0.353/0.463, 0.197/0.347, and 0.242/0.216 for D1–D3, respectively. Thus the D1/D2 direction reversal is explained by the genomic coverage changing: the full contig includes the distal part of In(17)4 beyond tree coverage, whereas the matched complement contains only the proximal part and collinear gaps/flanks. It is a distinct estimand, not a demonstrated computation error. The high contribution density and strongly heterogeneous interval-specific values make simple “inversion effect” language inappropriate.\n\nExact sample-ID gene-tree estimates are D_topology=q3−q2: +0.0785 (D1), −0.1613 (D2), +0.0705 (D3). Whole matched-span nucleotide D_site/topology correlations are positive at 50–500 kb (see `spatial_validation.tsv`; at 100 kb r=+0.688/+0.629/+0.711). These are descriptive spatial co-variation measures. Aggregate correlations can be driven partly by large inside/outside transitions; only 15 wholly collinear 100-kb bins occur in matched coverage, so a centered within-region comparison and outside-only inferential claim are weak. Circular shifts on a sparse, irregularly supported span do not supply a robust general spatial null. D relative to zero and inside-minus-outside D are separate questions.\n\nThe estimator and exact quartet calculations pass the documented synthetic checks. Population relationships and sampling structure mean the three frozen designs are exploratory, particularly D3's three carriers and its castaneus-versus-musculus species-history null. The indexed transversion/callability scan completed (65/65 chunks); exact tree-matched signs and interval contrasts were stable at all three call-rate thresholds. The individual-level scan did not complete: the remote endpoint truncated BGZF at file offset 48,567,409,620, and no leave-one-out or balanced-subset outputs are reported. No sample-level robustness claim is warranted. Most critically, unphased VCF genotypes and reconstructed pseudo-t tree tips represent different biological observations. No result is direct evidence about phased t-chromosome alleles or uniquely establishes introgression/MSRC.\n''')
(R/'manuscript_methods.md').write_text('''# Methods text\n\nWe analyzed the Harr et al. AllMouse PASS VCF on mouse chromosome 17, mm10/GRCm38, by indexed regional queries, using the pre-frozen 55 sample IDs and three P1/P2/P3/O population designs in `config/frozen_quartet_members.tsv` (D1 4/12/13/8; D2 8/13/12/8; D3 3/7/13/8). Only biallelic single-nucleotide A/C/G/T records were retained. Diploid `0/0`, `0/1`, and `1/1` GTs contributed ALT dosages 0, 1, and 2; population ALT frequency was the mean across completely called individuals, with incomplete calls omitted. At least one complete call per ingroup population was required. Outgroups were retained only when all eight *M. spretus* samples were complete and fixed for REF or ALT. Fixed-REF sites used ALT frequencies; fixed-ALT sites used derived-allele frequencies `1−ALT`. Polymorphic or missing outgroups were excluded.\n\nFor derived frequencies p1, p2, p3, per-site contributions were ABBA=`(1−p1)p2p3` and BABA=`p1(1−p2)p3`; contributions were pooled before calculating D=`(ABBA−BABA)/(ABBA+BABA)`. A zero denominator is undefined. VCF positions are one-based; assignment used `(POS−1)//window_size` to zero-based half-open windows. D was aggregated at 5, 50, 100, 250, and 500 kb. Tree window labels from Kelemen & Vicoso were restored by the documented +5 Mb offset; only exact overlapping intervals were compared. Published inversion coordinates were taken unchanged from the independent GRCm38/mm10 interval table.\n\nThe exact sample-ID tree comparison classified each induced four-tip combination once by four-point distances into q1=(P1,P2)|(P3,O), q2=(P1,P3)|(P2,O), q3=(P2,P3)|(P1,O); ties were unresolved. Within-tree frequencies were calculated among resolved quartets, each local tree was weighted equally, and D_topology=q3−q2. Quartet combinations are not independent loci. Pearson/Spearman spatial correlations and 500-kb block resampling are descriptive; intervals with sparse coverage and circular-shift p-values under irregular support are not treated as robust general spatial inference.\n\nThe VCF genotypes are unphased diploid calls. Local-tree carrier tips are reconstructed pseudo-t-haplotype sequences, not verified homolog-specific copies of the VCF calls. These estimands therefore do not constitute t-haplotype-specific nucleotide D. Population structure, geography, subspecies history, admixture, ancestral structure, incomplete lineage sorting, SNP ascertainment, and linked variation remain possible explanations.\n''')
(R/'figure_captions.md').write_text('''# Figure caption\n\n**Figure 1. Corrected chr17 nucleotide and exact gene-tree quartet tracks.** Four published t-complex inversion intervals are shown on the common mm10/GRCm38 chromosome-17 axis. Rows show the three frozen exploratory designs. The nucleotide panel plots corrected fixed-REF plus fixed-ALT population-level D in 100-kb bins; points are absent where no denominator exists. The exact matched topology panel plots equal-locus D_topology=q3−q2 only over chr17:5.0–37.055 Mb, the local-tree coverage. The informative-site panel reports nucleotide informative-site counts. Blank regions are unsupported, not interpolated. Full chromosome-17 estimates and matched-span estimates have different genomic coverage. The genotype and tree panels also represent different biological estimands because VCF calls are unphased diploids and carrier tree tips are reconstructed pseudo-t sequences.\n''')
(F/'README.md').write_text('''# House-mouse chr17 Patterson D final validation\n\nThis additive finalization preserves the frozen pipeline and prior results. `results/` distinguishes corrected fixed-REF+ALT D, superseded fixed-REF-only values, exact q3−q2 topology, full-contig vs physical-span vs exact-tree-matched contrasts, completed filter sensitivity, and incomplete sample-level sensitivity. Quartet and phasing audits are in `../results/final_validation/`.\n\nReproduction from repository root (environment: `.venv-malaria310`):\n\n```sh\n.venv-malaria310/bin/python empirical/house_mouse_t_complex/analysis/patterson_d/polarization_validation/tests/test_polarization.py\n.venv-malaria310/bin/python empirical/house_mouse_t_complex/analysis/patterson_d/exact_quartet_comparison/tests/test_quartet_scoring.py\n.venv-malaria310/bin/python empirical/house_mouse_t_complex/analysis/patterson_d/final_validation/tests/test_scalar_reference.py\n.venv-malaria310/bin/python empirical/house_mouse_t_complex/analysis/patterson_d/final_validation/scripts/build_final_validation.py\n```\n\nPrimary corrected scan reproduction is documented in `../README.md`; exact quartet reproduction is in `../exact_quartet_comparison/README.md`. Optional robustness retry command: `.venv-malaria310/bin/python empirical/house_mouse_t_complex/analysis/patterson_d/polarization_validation/scripts/robustness_scan.py`; it resumes complete chunk checkpoints; this run verified 65/65 chunks and generated the transversion and 80/90/100% call-rate results. Do not download the full 55.7-GB VCF. The separate sample-level scan was attempted but the endpoint truncated BGZF at byte offset 48,567,409,620 before outputs completed.\n\nPaper readiness: **CONDITIONAL GO** for a carefully framed population-level allele-sharing analysis with the filter sensitivity scan complete and sample-level influence flagged as unresolved; **not** ready as phased t-haplotype evidence.\n''')
